bazelbuild/bazel/blob/master/distdir_deps.bzl#L276-L278)), which dates from October 2020:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<Key>bazel_coverage_output_generator/releases/coverage_output_generator-v2.5.zip</Key>\r\n<Generation>1601544711356173</Generation>\r\n<MetaGeneration>1</MetaGeneration>\r\n<LastModified>2020-10-01T09:31:51.356Z</LastModified>\r\n<ETag>\"f2c7b30d375402c0083ad888e5add849\"</ETag>\r\n<Size>4221347</Size>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is missing some important fixes, eg #8731, resulting in not all files being included in the coverage output,\r\n\r\nCan a new version of the coverage_out_generator be published and the distribution updated to use it?\n\n### What's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\n\n\nn/a\n\n### Which operating system are you running Bazel on?\n\n\nLinux\n\n### What is the output of `bazel info release`?\n\n\nrelease 5.1.0\n\n### If `bazel info release` returns `development version` or `(@non-git)`, tell us how you built Bazel.\n\n\n_No response_\n\n### What's the output of `git remote get-url origin; git rev-parse master; git rev-parse HEAD` ?\n\n\n_No response_\n\n### Have you found anything relevant by searching the web?\n\n#11585 tracked an earlier instance of this same problem - the CoverageOutputGenerator package being stale.\n\n### Any other information, logs, or outputs that you want to share?\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/15396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/15396/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]